            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0844" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1162/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-19T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1926—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 19—6:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>290. My 186, April 20, 11 a.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d577-f1"/> Following from
                    American consul general at Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 18, noon. Reliable information just received that Chinese have
                            taken over American Baptist hospital at Wuchow which is now full of sick
                            and wounded soldiers. Further details later.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
